<article class="env-definition" id="0862">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0862">Definition <span data-tag="0862">71.18.1</span>.</a> With $Z \subset B$ and $f : X \to B$ as above. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Given a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$ the <em>strict transform</em> of $\mathcal{F}$ with respect to the blowup of $B$ in $Z$ is the quotient $\mathcal{F}'$ of $\text{pr}_ X^*\mathcal{F}$ by the submodule of sections supported on $|\text{pr}_{B'}^{-1}E|$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>strict transform</em> of $X$ is the closed subspace $X' \subset X \times _ B B'$ cut out by the quasi-coherent ideal of sections of $\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ B B'}$ supported on $|\text{pr}_{B'}^{-1}E|$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>